WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:09.834
Hi! We count shoes in twos and fingers in fives. Today we'll learn the 2, 5 and 10 times tables.

2
00:00:09.984 --> 00:00:15.954
The 2 times table is counting in twos: 2, 4, 6, 8, 10.

3
00:00:16.104 --> 00:00:21.162
7 twos make 14. 2 times 7 is 14.

4
00:00:21.312 --> 00:00:25.266
In the 10 times table, every answer ends in 0.

5
00:00:25.416 --> 00:00:29.010
8 tens make 80.

6
00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:36.138
The 5 times table is counting in fives: 5, 10, 15, 20, 25.

7
00:00:36.288 --> 00:00:40.410
In the 5 times table, answers end in 5 or 0.

8
00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:44.850
6 fives make 30, like 6 hands with 30 fingers.

9
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:53.298
Swapping the numbers doesn't change the answer: 3 times 5 and 5 times 3 are both 15.

10
00:00:53.448 --> 00:00:57.450
Watch out! 5 times 7 is not 30!

11
00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:07.098
Count in fives, 7 times: 5, 10, 15, 20, 25, 30, 35.

12
00:01:07.248 --> 00:01:11.730
So 5 times 7 is 35.

13
00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:19.842
Your turn! What is 2 times 9? Pause and think.

14
00:01:19.992 --> 00:01:25.290
9 twos make 18. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:33.570
Another one! What is 5 times 9? Pause and think.

16
00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:39.234
9 fives make 45. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:39.384 --> 00:01:47.442
Here's another! What is 10 times 6? Pause and think.

18
00:01:47.592 --> 00:01:52.938
6 tens make 60. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:53.088 --> 00:02:02.922
Try one more! 4 pairs of shoes. How many shoes altogether? Pause and think.

20
00:02:03.072 --> 00:02:09.978
Each pair has 2, so 4 times 2 is 8 shoes. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:10.128 --> 00:02:20.538
Try one more! There are 5 buns in each pack. How many in 7 packs? Pause and think.

22
00:02:20.688 --> 00:02:26.898
7 times 5 is 35 buns. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:27.048 --> 00:02:35.130
Try one more! What is 10 times 6? Pause and think.

24
00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:41.490
6 tens is 60; it ends in 0. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:52.170
Last one! 8 children get 5 sweets each. How many sweets altogether? Pause and think.

26
00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:58.698
8 fives: 5 times 8 is 40. Did you get it right?

27
00:02:58.848 --> 00:03:08.754
Remember: count in twos, fives and tens. 10s end in 0, 5s end in 5 or 0, and swapping the numbers doesn't change the answer.

28
00:03:08.904 --> 00:03:14.345
Take turns saying the 5 times table with your family today!

